{"name":"Moray","hex":"#c8bd6a","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Moray","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A historical county in northern Scotland, absorbed into Grampian Region in 1975.","A local government district in Grampian Region from 1975 until Grampian Region's abolition in 1996."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Moray"}],"entries":[{"title":"Moray","blocks":[{"text":"Moray is one of the 32 council areas of Scotland. It lies in the north-east of the country, with a coastline on the Moray Firth, and borders the council areas of Aberdeenshire and Highland. Its council is based in Elgin, the area's largest town. The main towns are generally in the north of the area on the coastal plain. The south of the area is more sparsely populated and mountainous, including part of the Cairngorms National Park."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7a/Moray_UK_location_map.svg/330px-Moray_UK_location_map.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Moray","wikidata":"Q211106"},{"title":"Moray (UK Parliament constituency)","blocks":[{"text":"Moray was a county constituency of the House of Commons of the Parliament of the United Kingdom. It elected one Member of Parliament (MP) by the first past the post system of election."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0f/MorayConstituency.svg/330px-MorayConstituency.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Moray_(UK_Parliament_constituency)","wikidata":"Q1053311"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/ca/Employmentmoray.png/500px-Employmentmoray.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/ca/Employmentmoray.png/500px-Employmentmoray.png?utm_source=en